# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 sym2poly.cc sym2rxrootnum, the root pick of normal and simplify for a d-th root of an expression (X^d-num). The pick compares arg(root) with arg(evalf(num))/d. (1) On the cut (num a negative real) the arg came from evalf(num), whose rounding imaginary part chose its sign: z=acosh(-1/2) is ln((i*sqrt(3)-1)/2), whose evalf has a real part of -1e-15, so evalf(z^2) had arg -pi; now an imaginary part that recursive_normal proves 0 gives arg +pi, else its sign at Digits+20, +40, ... +1280 where it is clear of the rounding. (2) For a square root the two roots X-r, X+r both scored near 0 (d*arg(root)-arg(num) is a multiple of 2*pi for every root), v was replaced by the first chosen factor so the second root was scored with d=1, and the fix of the argument by a root of unity never runs for d=2 (-1 is no polynomial): simplify(sqrt(acosh(-1/2)^2)) gave -ln((i*sqrt(3)-1)/2), about -2.0944*i (right +2.0944*i, the principal root of -4*pi^2/9), also acosh(-1/3). Now for d=2 both roots are scored with d=2 and the principal root (arg(root) = arg(num)/2) is taken.
